# Answering one ask must not discard the one raised after it.
#
# Drop authority used to be keyed by SESSION: resolving an ask stamped the
# whole thread, and every load already in flight for it was thrown away whole.
# During a live turn the in-flight load is exactly the one carrying the agent's
# NEXT question, so answering the first discarded the second.
#
# The empty gap between the two made it permanent. An attach snapshot with no
# asks erased the session from attachAsks and stamped it, and the periodic
# sweep only visits threads it already holds asks for -- so after the gap
# nothing was left to ask again, and the second question never arrived at all.
#
# The `raised` fixture is that sequence, deterministically: an approval, then
# two reads with nothing pending, then a second question. It needs no
# HANABI_ASK_FAIL --- the resolve has to actually succeed for drop_attach_ask
# to run, which is the code under test.
#
# settings: {"window_width":760,"window_height":620,"open_tabs":["t2"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_ASK_DEMO=raised HANABI_ASK_REFRESH_SECS=0.2

require_thread t2
expect_text "The agent needs approval"
expect_text "bash may write outside the workspace; a human has to allow it."

click_ui ask_submit
wait_frames 30

# The first ask is answered and gone.
expect_no_text "bash may write outside the workspace; a human has to allow it."

# Through the empty gap and out the other side: the sweep kept watching, so
# the question raised after the answer arrives.
wait_frames 200
expect_text "One more before I run it: which cycle books the correction?"

# It is a real card, not a husk: answer it.
click_ui ask_text_q3
wait_frames 4
type "book it against 2026-09"
wait_frames 6
expect_input_text ask_text_q3 "book it against 2026-09"

# ...and the draft and the card's identity both survive the sweeps that keep
# arriving underneath it. A refresh that re-adopted the ask under a new
# identity would drop the answer on the floor here.
wait_frames 120
expect_text "One more before I run it: which cycle books the correction?"
expect_input_text ask_text_q3 "book it against 2026-09"
expect_no_text "Answer to submit"
